=2 Walkthrough
* Speak to {n:Bki Tbujhja} to begin the quest; she will request a {i:flask of holy water|Holy Water|4154}.
* Trade Bki Tbujhja the {i:Holy Water|Holy Water|4154} and you will be asked to travel to {z:The Eldieme Necropolis} and to visit the tomb of a great bard of yesteryear. Once there you are to purify the tomb and play the requiem. She returns the flask of holy water and sends you on your way.
** (Optional) Speak to Malatigeat at the meadhouse for more information on this 'great bard of yesteryear'.

>**From this point on, the quest can be completed on any job.**
* Travel to {z:The Eldieme Necropolis} via (F-5) in {z:Batallia Downs} and head for a room with five unbroken sarcophagi at D-4.
** You will have to travel through {z:Beaucedine Glacier} to reach the barrow containing the proper entrance to the Necropolis complex.
** If you have unlocked the {p:Lycopodium (NPC)} teleport service for {z:Batallia Downs}, trading one of the accepted flowers to the sparkling light (blank target) at (F-5) teleports the player to the elevated portion of the map.
** The quickest way is to take the {p:Voidwatch} warp to {z:Beaucedine Glacier}.
*** {z:Beaucedine Glacier} - {p:Unity Warp} will take you near it.
* Trade the flask of Holy Water to the sarcophagus to spawn three skeleton NMs. The sarcophagus that will spawn the NMs is random.
** Side with three, one closest to the exit door
* Defeat all three NMs that spawn, then interact with the same sarcophagus again. You will get a cutscene and receive the {@k} {p:Star ring (tarnished)}.
** If you have multiple people doing this quest, they can trade their holy water to the correct sarcophagus after the fight and they will get the cutscene and ring.
* Return to Bki Tbujhja and receive your **{i:Choral Slippers|Choral Slippers|14098}**.

=2 Field Notes
The three NM skeletons that spawn are as follows:
* Yum Kimil (BLM)
* Dog Guardian
* Owl Guardian

The two Guardian skeletons are roughly lvl 50-55, where as Yum Kimil is likely 60-65. They are all highly resistant to Lullaby, even with a 75 Bard. A standard geared White Mage at 75 was able to Repose the Guardians without any trouble at all for the full sleep duration. Two level 75 characters should have little difficulty defeating the NMs.{br} You do not need to be on Bard to activate the NMs or receive the cutscene.
